                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "if someone tried to start a full sync and the network was down, how would that show up?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Control/SyncBMCData.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harsh Agarwal",
                        "email": "harsh.agarwal@ibm.com",
                        "username": "harsh-agarwal1"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you mean, before starting a full sync, or after starting?\nBefore starting: we would indicate that the sibling is not available.\nAfter starting: the exact reason for the failure would be unclear (as concurrent process, though some data may still pass). To address this, added a \"FullSyncFailed\" status. This status allows us to identify that some data may have failed during the sync process."
                }
